<h2 id="architecture-briefly">Architecture, briefly</h2>

<p>A 32-pixel encoder lays out the image and passes its tokens to a 16-pixel decoder that predicts
image and code together. The loss is a single velocity objective against targets \(x\) and \(c(x)\),
with DINOv2 frozen throughout — it is used to define the path, never trained.</p>

